# Local development snapshots. `npm run dev` and `astro build` copy anything
# under `public/` verbatim into `dist/`, and the page fetches `/data/status.json`
# at runtime — so a snapshot committed here would be served to residents as the
# current state, with a timestamp that stops being true the moment it lands.
# The real one comes from S3 through the Amplify rewrite. Regenerate locally with:
#   RAIN_ALERT_SNAPSHOT_PATH=web/public/data/status.json uv run rain-alert-cycle --offline-fixtures <dir>
public/data/
